  "body": "## The bug you reported\n\nv5.3.0 hardcoded `ENABLE_WEB_SERVER_TOOLS=true` on the `mcc-claude` / `fcc-claude` child env. That was **half a switch**:\n\n- The client told Claude Code to offer `web_search`/`web_fetch` tools.\n- But the **proxy's own** `enable_web_server_tools` (which gates local execution) was still **off by default** in the settings model.\n\nSo via `mcc-claude` a web_search call hit *\"local web server tools are disabled (ENABLE_WEB_SERVER_TOOLS=false)\"* — the exact error you saw. Your manual `settings.json` path worked because that environment's `.env` had the var on.\n\n## The fix\n\n1. **`launch()` now passes `settings.enable_web_server_tools`** into the env builder, which sets `ENABLE_WEB_SERVER_TOOLS=true` on the session **only when the proxy will actually execute the tools**. The dashboard **Web Tools** toggle now controls both layers with one switch.\n2. **Settings default flipped `false` → `true`.** The code default contradicted `.env.example`, the dashboard manifest, and `mcc-init`'s env template (all `true`). The `false` was only a wrong fallback when no `.env` existed.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `build_minimal_claude_proxy_env` omits the var by default, adds exactly it when `enable_web_server_tools=True`.\n- New launcher test: setting off → no env var, only proxy vars changed.\n- Two default-contract tests updated to expect `true`; the \"rejects forced server tool when disabled\" API test now explicitly disables the setting.\n- 368 tests pass; the 2 `test_web_server_tools.py` failures are pre-existing on unmodified `fork/main` (confirmed earlier).\n- ruff format/check and ty clean.\n\nVersion 5.3.0 → 5.3.1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
