    "message": "fix(claude): make mcc-claude web-tools flag mirror the proxy setting; default the setting to on\n\nv5.3.0 hardcoded ENABLE_WEB_SERVER_TOOLS=true on the mcc-claude / fcc-claude\nchild env. That was half a switch: the client advertised web_search/web_fetch to\nthe model, but the proxy's own enable_web_server_tools setting (which gates local\nexecution) was still off by default in the settings model, so a web_search call\nvia mcc-claude hit the \"local web server tools are disabled\" error -- while the\nmanual settings.json path worked because that environment's .env had the var on.\n\nThe launcher now passes settings.enable_web_server_tools into\nbuild_minimal_claude_proxy_env, which sets ENABLE_WEB_SERVER_TOOLS=true on the\nsession only when the proxy will actually execute the tools. One switch -- the\ndashboard Web Tools toggle -- now controls both layers.\n\nThe settings default was also false while .env.example, the dashboard manifest,\nand mcc-init's env template all ship true, so the code default only mattered as\na wrong fallback when no .env existed. Flips it to true and corrects the comment.\n\nTests: build_minimal_claude_proxy_env now omits the var by default and adds\nexactly it when enabled; a new launcher test covers the off path (no env var,\nonly proxy vars changed); the two default-contract tests updated to expect true;\nthe \"rejects forced server tool when disabled\" API test now explicitly disables\nthe setting. 368 pass; the 2 test_web_server_tools failures are pre-existing on\nunmodified fork/main. ruff/ty clean.\n\nVersion 5.3.0 -> 5.3.1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
